      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T02:01:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you are using MGLRU then the flush is not required in any situation.\nIf you are not using MGLRU and you are performing a similar calculation to `workingset_test_recent` that requires estimating the workingset size based on `NR_{IN}ACTIVE_FILE/ANON` then flushing would be required to get the most recent data. However since `workingset_refault` -\u003e `workingset_test_recent` already flushes the line before `trace_android_vh_refault_filemap_add_folio`, I don\u0027t think you\u0027ll gain much by manually flushing again inside the tracepoint, especially with this ratelimited version of the flush.",
